  triage:title "Ack parity case is a conditional pass-through on an optional fixture field, not the twin-message requires_ack scenario deliverable 3 / AC6 requires" ;
  triage:description "qa-pr1184-r1 req-qa (confirmed): the ack case in crates/atm-graft-python/tests/test_cli_parity.py is only: ack_message_id = fixture.get(ack_message_id); if not None then ack. Nothing creates a second identity, sends a requires_ack message, makes a twin, or asserts pending_ack absence afterwards, contrary to deliverable 3 and AC6 in docs/plans/phase-aw/sprint-AW.5-native-tool-parity.md. Fix: implement the full scenario and the pending_ack-absence assertion. CLOSURE (2026-09-05T05:30:00Z): r2 verified fixed: req-qa/arch-qa/rust-qa-agent all confirm resolved at b7fbf54e64." ;
